{"title":"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(very_long)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (very long)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>(a)</b> Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b063495d0243e7bc52c3a7f231362bdc4a03775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><b>(b)</b> Prove that there is no positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb810ba5d07f7078bea65c2ae90edf15e09874f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rap6C3ks29s\">https://youtu.be/rap6C3ks29s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/974dd5ab40d406571bdb8c99b8503f16cb1e1b6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e9a092417fc5007f15fbeca7054c70cdbd1d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d524c51b59647866bc337983e45d54471e743a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, respectively.\n</p><p><b>(a)</b> From the statement above, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will work.\n</p><p><b>(b)</b> Again from the statement above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> can never be congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e9a092417fc5007f15fbeca7054c70cdbd1d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, so there are no solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>This solution is clearer and easier to understand.\n</p><p>(1) Since we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b063495d0243e7bc52c3a7f231362bdc4a03775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is congruent to 0 (mod 7), we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is congruent to 8 mod 7, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is congruent to 1 mod 7.\n</p><p>Experimenting with the residue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> mod 7: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />=1: 2\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />=2: 4\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />=3: 1 (this is because when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is doubled to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e17b512a68cae66ced6cd686e726193d7a27eedc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2*2^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, the residue doubles too, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d8532fea6e90aca51de5a596c8914b62863d4407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4*2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> is congruent to 1 (mod 7).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />=4: 2\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />=5: 4\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />=6: 1\n</p><p>Through induction, we easily show that this is true since the residue doubles every time you double <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>So, the residue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> mod 7 cycles in 2, 4, 1. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be a multiple of 3. Proved.\n</p><p>(2) According to part (1), the residue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> cycles in 2, 4, 1. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb810ba5d07f7078bea65c2ae90edf15e09874f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> is congruent to 0 mod 7, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> must be congruent to 6 mod 7, but this is not possible due to how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> mod 7 cycles. Therefore, there is no solution. Proved.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/2/432ff4086dae85c162bbcfeaa3463f1750fddf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3m + r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/a/15afb5ee1fe5338d86cf4fd322042273048e7fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\in \\{0,1,2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/9810fcd0e28d9dc105e769d04a50f8b5d7ae56b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in \\mathbb{N}_{\\geq 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"71\" height=\"19\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c121dfcd70a0d338d3c9bbbb9ab1d93ecab74173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n - 1 \\equiv_7 2^r - 1 \\equiv_7 0 \\iff r = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"17\" />. Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17fa82e0bd83cb5fec2b61d34aeb13c9eb775fc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n+1 \\equiv_7 2^r + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" /> which can only be equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac8effbba9c83e52fc90ea5a0c3269f872dbbbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28very_long.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(very_long)\">Solution 3 (very long)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (very long)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution\n</p><p>Part 1: We test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2716095563023b9bb6472d0006749d945c2039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> and find that the first statement is equivalent to testing out which powers of two are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547b813e997d4a054fbc9ab1f04bc1c5b93cd67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. However, the difference of powers factorization makes this more simple; for this is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/306c74fa437742e4c42ec20865e37c3ded74d150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n-1^n=(2-1)(2^{n-1}+2^{n-2}+2^{n-3}+...+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"372\" height=\"21\" />. Simping gives the statement that the sum of all of the powers of two before a number must equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530257b39008ad9abc4a7b10631ef029f2aa4389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />. Testing small integers gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> work, but there must be a proof.\n</p><p>Here's where the proof comes in: we claim that all of the possible integers that satisfy Part 1 are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bef523fd84a18941d31804f9293b436bdfdf6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{multiples of 3.}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"117\" height=\"28\" />\nTo solve this problem, we look into the base-2 representation of the numbers. The problem statement states that all of the numbers are in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b3490dc63da292044a21584bc6c3d9a48645d69e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111...1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />. One can even look more detailed into binary representation; the first \"digit\" represents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f697cd56b20fb242120d479824db503058069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^0$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, the second \"digit\"; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e68ad31d12ba3d14b80a9341ee44e6238555124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, and the third \"digit\"; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. These are equal to 1, 2, and 4, respectively, which means that their <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2716095563023b9bb6472d0006749d945c2039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />s are 1, 2, and 4, respectively. However, something interesting begins to happen at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a4ab443c94f13ae3ad0efbc8c6fa07b58a930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />; its decimal representation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so it leaves a remainder of 1 when divided by 7. The structure of binary digits consistently repeating means that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4461877e328edd4298545f51c7d8d170bd3bed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod 7$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" /> representation for each digit loops every three times. To make a multpile of 7, the sum of the mods must also add up to a multpile of 7, which is satisfied for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d1eed7be2e1dcbfd4f7fe86fba2eb7566d8bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47ed4a18a2c33a6521754c173a4135f95835cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+2+1=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />, using digit representation. Interestingly, this works for any number of ones, if it is a multiple of 3, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73b45e2451704482e4948213428b224c2799e578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111111=4+2+1+4+2+1=14=0\\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"394\" height=\"20\" />. This means that all integer multiples of 3 work.\n</p><p>Prooving all non-multpiles of 3 DON't work is trivialized: if the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d0293089c9d37a2fc8c65feca5b66fb60ea1c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, this means that there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee51c225f028dce11948ae5a5ee71a77477d88c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+4+2+1+4+2+1+...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"236\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856cd8dc4a4efdfafa2d5d5c514f6b9046ff8beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+7+7+...+7=1+0+0+0...\\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"357\" height=\"20\" />, which is not a multiple of 7. Likewise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/14993088c90e11f704b76e68891cac3a83f0389a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> also doesn't work, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/3916a3818b35b2e037e5dddb992b6110fd3c7ee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+1+4+2+1+...=2+1+7+...+7=2+1+0+0+0...=3 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"617\" height=\"20\" />. This proves that all numbers that are multiples of 3 work.\n</p><p>Part 2: Binary also can solve this problem. One can use Part 1's mod results to solve this problem. In the problem statement, it is given that the number is in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57a3863d56a827a4188f7ec3d851dee9e94b8714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10000...001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />, where the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s in between is integer. Using the Part 1 proof, it is given that the mod 7 for each power of two minus one loops every three numbers, so we use those as cases.\n</p><p>Case 1: The number of sandwiched zeroes is a multpile of 3.\nSubtracting two from this number gives a number in the format <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1afba101fba7d0793e8e0558a64d3737095ec7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11111...111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />, where the number of ones is equal to one more than a multpile of 3. By Part 1 of this proof, this number in mod 7 form is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547b813e997d4a054fbc9ab1f04bc1c5b93cd67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. Adding two to this number to create a number in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf319ef22ccc07db00ad18777f4285f3ca04212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000...01$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> form results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e813f2430b76402d67161c6f735da374f9c87797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, which is not a multpipe.\n</p><p>Case 2: The number of sandwiched zeroes is one more than a multpile of 3.\nThis makes the number of ones equal to two more than a multpile of 3, when this number is subtracted by 2, making the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/2339352d4ff20ab915d68f7e7007e8cc80f7fbba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1111...111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" /> representation congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e813f2430b76402d67161c6f735da374f9c87797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. Adding back two gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3212c9f8de571676ae99c1bdcee7ba94011c10ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, which is also not a multpile.\n</p><p>Case 3: The number of zeroes is two more than a multpile.\nThis makes the number of ones equal to a multpile of 3, when this number is subtracted by 2, making the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/2339352d4ff20ab915d68f7e7007e8cc80f7fbba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1111...111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" /> representation congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530257b39008ad9abc4a7b10631ef029f2aa4389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />. Adding back two gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6e91e2975ab3c40bb695826a3fd4c3047c65d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, which is also not a multpile.\n</p><p>An integer must fit into one of these cases, none of which result in a multpile of 7. This means that it is impossible for a number in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb810ba5d07f7078bea65c2ae90edf15e09874f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> congruent to 0 mod 7, or, in other words, be a multpile of 7. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5aUMLGgmGy0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5aUMLGgmGy0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO\" title=\"1964 IMO\">1964 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017073716\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 482/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 867/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14995/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.525      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.525      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wik